WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.009
Every job has that one coworker everyone avoids
like the plague.

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:08.730
Well, it turns out that working in Hollywood
is just like any other job, and some celebrities

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.849
have earned a serious reputation among their
co-stars—so much so, that other actors don't

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:16.100
ever want to work with them again.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.660
Let's take a look at some of the most infamous
co-star beefs, and how they got started.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.060
Julia Roberts vs Nick Nolte

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:28.450
Costars in the 1994 romcom I Love Trouble,
Roberts and Nolte didn't mesh well onscreen

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.700
or off.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.360
Reportedly, the constant quarreling got so
bad that director Charles Shyer resorted to

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.140
filming some of their scenes separately to
keep them apart as much as possible.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.560
"You have zero chance of scoring here, trust
me, move on."

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.140
"I'm sorry, where did you say you're from,
Bitchville?"

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.900
While shooting, Roberts told the New York
Times that Nolte was...

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.760
"Completely disgusting [and] seems go out
of his way to repel people."

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.149
Nolte later shot back,

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:55.329
"It's not nice to call someone 'disgusting.'

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:57.170
But she's not a nice person.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.170
Everyone knows that."

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.000
James Franco vs Tyrese Gibson

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.970
Much of the 2006 military drama Annapolis
centers around a planned boxing tournament

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.250
for the U.S. Naval Academy.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:13.750
"There ain't no way I'm letting someone finish
this year, whose not worthy of this academy."

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.600
"I'm not quitting."

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.290
But Franco took his method acting way too
far.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:23.299
According to co-star Tyrese Gibson, Franco
actually landed punches during rehearsal.

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:24.390
Gibson told Elle,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.180
"The dude was full-on hitting me.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.340
I was always like, 'James, lighten up, man.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.369
We're just practicing.'

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.700
He never lightened up."

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.680
Franco denies ever hitting Gibson, but admitted
to GQ,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.380
"I was probably a jerk."

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.930
But the admission wasn't good enough for Gibson,
who told Playboy in 2007,

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:42.780
"I never want to work with him again, and
I'm sure he feels the same way.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.920
It felt very personal.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.580
It was f—ed up."

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.049
Shannen Doherty vs everyone

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:52.619
The notoriously difficult Shannen Doherty
reportedly nearly came to blows with her Beverly

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:55.810
Hills 90210 castmate Jennie Garth.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:01.869
Fighting became so bad that fellow 90210 vet
Tori Spelling revealed to Lifetime in 2015

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:06.960
that she even got her father, Aaron Spelling,
who produced the show, to fire Doherty.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.090
Then, four years later, Doherty and castmate
Alyssa Milano beefed on the set of another

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.349
Aaron Spelling production, Charmed.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:15.349
According to Milano,

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:19.510
"There were definitely some rough days…
it was very much sort of like high school."

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:24.260
Over a decade has passed since Doherty's departure
from Charmed, and it seems she and Milano

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.180
have finally buried the hatchet.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:30.569
When Doherty was diagnosed with breast cancer
in 2016, Milano said,

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:38.090
"I told her my concern and how everyone was
on her side and we're all supporting her,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.560
and she was very appreciative that I reached
out."

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.360
Richard Gere vs Sylvester Stallone

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.760
For years, there's been an apparent behind-the-scenes
feud between Gere and Stallone.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.770
Stallone finally explained the beef between
the actors with Ain't It Cool News in 2006,

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:58.260
saying Gere had originally been cast as the
lead in 1974's The Lords of Flatbush.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.030
But since Gere and Stallone clashed immediately
during filming, Gere was replaced by Perry

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.030
King.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:08.110
Stallone recalls Gere getting too rough during
fight rehearsals and spilling greasy food

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.720
all over Stallone's pants.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.720
Sly claims,

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.740
"To this day he seriously dislikes me.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.540
He even thinks I'm the individual responsible
for the gerbil rumor.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.990
Not true… but that's the rumor."

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:23.190
"Just relax, amigo, you wanna talk, we'll
talk.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.890
I'm a sucker for good conversation"

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.629
Robert Downey Jr. vs Terrence Howard

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:33.070
Howard isn't shy about talking about his falling
out with Iron Man co-star Robert Downey Jr.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.660
"I'm not mad, I'm indifferent."

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:41.340
"I told him I was sorry, you don't respect
yourself so I know you don't respect me."

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.709
In 2013, Howard appeared on Watch What Happens
Live, and claimed that while the studio had

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:47.730
initially signed him to a three-movie deal,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.790
"They came to me with the second and said
'Look, we will pay you one-eighth of what

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:58.250
we contractually had for you, because we think
the second one will be successful with or

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.250
without you."

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.550
He went on to blame Downey, a.k.a., the former
"friend" whom he'd helped book Iron Man in

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.690
the first place.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:10.030
"I called my friend, that I helped get the
first job, and he didn't call me back for

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.030
three months."

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:16.390
Three years later, the pair finally patched
things up and reunited at the 2016 wedding

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.459
of director Brian Grazer.

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:21.019
Kevin Smith vs Bruce Willis

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:25.389
While Smith and Willis had no issues acting
together in Live Free or Die Hard, the two

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:29.990
hit the skids on the set of 2010's Cop Out,
in which Willis starred and Smith directed.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.180
Smith had even taken a massive pay cut in
order to work with Willis on the film.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:37.499
But unfortunately, superstars sometimes come
with super egos.

00:04:37.499 --> 00:04:39.539
"It just went south.

00:04:39.539 --> 00:04:40.759
Right away.

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:43.650
The whole thing went south, Jack."

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.050
Smith later described the Cop Out directing
experience with Willis as "soul-crushing"

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.830
and credits Willis' co-star Tracy Morgan with
helping him get through filming:

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.749
"Were it not for Tracy, I might've killed
myself or someone else in the making of that

00:04:55.749 --> 00:04:56.340
movie."

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:00.740
"He's just talkin, talkin talkin, and the
whole time I'm thinking, that's David f---ing

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.900
Addison, man"

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.960
In his 2012 memoir Tough Sh*t, Smith said
that Willis,

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.909
"Turned out to be the unhappiest, most bitter,
and meanest emo-b*tch I've ever met at any

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:12.210
job I've held down.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.319
And mind you, I've worked at Domino's Pizza."

00:05:14.319 --> 00:05:16.159
Ouch.

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:19.439
Julianna Margulies vs Archie Panjabi

00:05:19.439 --> 00:05:24.379
On the set of The Good Wife, an ongoing feud
between stars Julianna Margulies and Archie

00:05:24.379 --> 00:05:28.189
Panjabi caused tension for years before Panjabi
left the show.

00:05:28.189 --> 00:05:31.719
While their characters were close friends,
the actresses were not.

00:05:31.719 --> 00:05:33.229
"I don't have friends."

00:05:33.229 --> 00:05:36.009
"You were a friend, and you lied to me."

00:05:36.009 --> 00:05:40.940
The pair were not actually filmed together
for a whopping 51 episodes, and most on-screen

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.169
communication between their characters took
place over the phone.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:48.909
When Panjabi left the show, she and Margulies
finally had a scene together, but, yep, it

00:05:48.909 --> 00:05:52.729
was also filmed separately, with some crafty
post-production.

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:55.569
Bette Davis vs Joan Crawford

00:05:55.569 --> 00:06:00.300
It was one of the most famous Hollywood rivalries
of all time—so much so that FX even developed

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.050
a series centered on the feud.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.129
"And action!"

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.759
"Oww, god damn!"

00:06:04.759 --> 00:06:06.939
"I barely touched her."

00:06:06.939 --> 00:06:11.779
These two queens of the silver screen had
it in for each other as early as the 1930s,

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:15.639
when Davis starred in the film Dangerous alongside
Franchot Tone.

00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:20.229
Davis was soon smitten with the actor, but
Crawford won that round, marrying Tone soon

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:22.220
after the movie wrapped production.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.159
Later, Davis famously remarked,

00:06:24.159 --> 00:06:27.830
"[Crawford] slept with every male star at
MGM except Lassie."

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:33.060
The rivalry came to a fever pitch in the 1960s,
when Davis and Crawford co-starred in Whatever

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.399
Happened to Baby Jane?

00:06:34.399 --> 00:06:38.490
When only Davis was nominated for an Oscar
for her role in the film, Crawford was livid.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.250
"God I hate this night!"

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.509
Crawford campaigned against Davis and managed
to steal the limelight for herself—when

00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:49.869
she accepted the Oscar on behalf of winner
Anne Bancroft, who was unable to attend the

00:06:49.869 --> 00:06:50.869
ceremony.

00:06:50.869 --> 00:06:54.949
Producer William Frye recalled Davis' reaction
at an Oscars after-party.

00:06:54.949 --> 00:06:58.949
Davis filled a glass with scotch all the way
to the rim, telling Frye it was for Crawford.

00:06:58.949 --> 00:07:03.179
When Frye told her that Crawford drank vodka,
and not scotch, Davis replied,

00:07:03.179 --> 00:07:04.879
"I don't care what she drinks.

00:07:04.879 --> 00:07:06.559
This is going into her f—ing face."

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:07.889
Thanks for watching!

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:10.539
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:10.539 --> 00:07:12.860
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

